module anon_ctor.pos_3

// A newtype's construction takes its REPRESENTATION (registry №1705):
// `Wrap({ n: 1 })` types the anonymous construction as `Bag` -- the
// newtype has no callable row of its own, so the argument met no
// expectation at all and reached the lattice unsettled, the ice this wave
// removes. The construction is judged against the representation and
// recorded, and `@record_newtype_ctor` accepts it as exactly the
// representation, as it does a named one.
//
// The program prints `ok`; observing the VALUE through the newtype
// (`w.n`) is outside the ORACLE's own codegen today ("anonymous record
// literal without spread not supported in codegen", measured 2026-10-31),
// so byte-for-byte agreement with the oracle stops at the construction
// itself -- which is what this fixture pins.
//
// The oracle builds and runs this file byte-for-byte the same (prints ok).
type Bag { n int }
type Wrap Bag

fn mk() -> Wrap => Wrap({ n: 1 })

fn main() {
    ro w = mk()
    println("ok")
}
